    "content": "Cori Close is the head coach of the UCLA Women's Basketball team, a position she has held since April 21, 2011. She recently led the Bruins to their first NCAA National Championship in program history, defeating South Carolina in 2026. She is known as a high-level recruiter and cultural builder, having guided the team to numerous NCAA tournament appearances and the 2025 Big Ten Tournament title. Key Details About Cori Close Position: The Michael Price Family UCLA Women's Head Basketball Coach. Tenure: Named head coach on April 21, 2011. Accomplishments: Led UCLA to the 2026 NCAA Championship, the first in school history. 2024-25 Season: Led the Bruins to a 34-3 record, the Final Four, and swept National Coach of the Year awards (AP, Naismith, USBWA, WBCA). Career Record: As of April 2026, she is over 300 wins at UCLA, becoming only the third coach in program history to reach 200 wins. Coaching Style: Highly regarded for developing team culture and player character, often citing influence from John Wooden. Previous Experience: Served as associate head coach at Florida State (2004–2011). 2025-26 Coaching Staff Tony Newnan: Associate Head Coach. Tasha Brown: Assistant Coach. Soh Matsuura: Assistant Coach. James Clark: Assistant Coach. Michaela Onyenwere: Assistant Coach. For more information, you can visit the UCLA Women's Basketball roster page. UCLA Women's Basketball roster page",
